(<ab>epic.</ab> <ab>Ā.</ab> as {#rAvaRo#}
 {#nArhate pUjAm#} <ls>Rām.</ls>)
.²1 To deserve, merit, be worthy of (with <ab>acc.</ab> or <ab>inf.</ab>); {#kimiva nAyuzmAnamareSvarAnnArhati#}
 <ls>Ś. 7</ls>; so {#daRqam, prAyaScittam, vaDam#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 To have a right to, be entitled to, be allowed to do anything (with
 <ab>acc.</ab>); {#nanu garBaH pitryaM rikTamarhati#} <ls>Ś. 6</ls>; {#na strI svAtantryamarhati#}
 <ls>Ms. 9. 3</ls>; also with <ab>inf.</ab> {#na sa tallabDumarhati#} <ls>Ms. 8. 147</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">11. 7</ls>, <ls n="Ms. 11.">18</ls>.
.²3 To be obliged or required to do a thing, <ab>oft.</ab> implying duty or obligation;
 {#nAnyatstrI dAtumarhati#} <ls>Y. 2. 49</ls>; {#imAM prasAdayitumarhasi#} <ls>R. 1. 88</ls>.
.²4 To be fit or deserve to be done; {#arTanA mayi BavadBiH kartumarhati#}
 <ls>N. 5. 112</ls>; <ls>Dk. 137</ls>.
.²5 To be equal to, be worth, {#na te gAtrARyupacAramarhanti#} <ls>Ś. 3. 17</ls>
 are not equal to; {#sarve te japayajYasya kalAM nArhanti zoqaSIm#} <ls>Ms. 2. 86</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">3. 131</ls>.
.²6 To be able, translatable by, ‘can’; {#na me vacanamanyaTA Bavitumarhati#}
 <ls>Ś. 4</ls>; {#vinASamavyayasyAsya na kaScitkartumarhati#} <ls>Bg. 2. 17</ls>; {#anudyogena#}
 {#tElAni tileByo nAptumarhati#} <ls>H. Pr. 30</ls> cannot get.
.²7 To worship, honour; see {%<ab>caus.</ab>%} below.
